  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 110 PM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nHot and dry conditions will continue across West Central Texas \nthrough the upcoming weekend into early next week, as the upper \nridge remains the dominant feature. For Friday and Saturday, \nslightly cooler temperatures are expected across the southern and \nsoutheastern counties, as low level moisture increases some due to\nthe remnants of Tropical Storm Bertha tracking westward across \nsouth Texas as it dissipates. The upper ridge will also shift a \nbit westward into New Mexico and far West Texas during this time \nframe, with the hottest temperatures expected across the Concho \nValley and Big Country. Heat Advisories will be possible from the \nConcho Valley into the Big Country both days.\n\nTemperatures will increase again areawide Sunday into early next \nweek, as the upper ridge expands eastward across Texas. \nTemperatures are expected to climb back into the upper 90s across \nsouthern portions of the forecast area and between 100 and 105 \ndegrees from the Concho Valley into the Big Country. Thus, Heat \nAdvisories will likely be needed across portions of the area once\nagain.",
